(156566,'https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3ASimple_Spaghetti','en','CC-BY-SA-3.0','Wikibooks — Cookbook:Simple Spaghetti','italian',NULL,1,'Adding salt to the cooking water enhances the pasta flavor and to allows the water to boil more quickly. Adding vegetable oil to the cooking water helps prevent the spaghetti from sticking together.
Try adding herbs or fruit (such as pineapple tidbits) to the water before it boils to keep with the pasta after straining for extra flavor and texture.
Before cooking the sauce, consider sautéing some finely minced onions, garlic, ground beef (or pork/sausage/veal/etc.), cheese (parmesan/mozzarella/etc.), mushrooms, or anything else that catches your fancy. Then add the sauce.
In a pinch, you can make plain spaghetti and add ketchup if you do not have any pasta sauce available.
The following foods go well with spaghetti and can be served together:
Broccoli (or other vegetables).
Garlic Bread
Meatballs
Pineapple (or other fruits) tidbits (boiled, grilled, or fried)
Shredded and/or grated cheese
Tomato, alfredo, or other sauces (can choose one, the other, or mixed together)
Cooking is about experimentation—never be afraid to try anything once!','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c6/Spaghetti_served_with_meat_sauce.jpg',640,427,'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spaghetti_served_with_meat_sauce.jpg','Original uploader was 酒池肉林 at zh.wikipedia','CC BY-SA 3.0',NULL,30,4,0,210.92,7.57,0.89,0.13,42.42,1.54,6.01,31.66,'B',75,1),
