You can use whole wheat or other traditional bread flours (e.g., rye) for part of the all-purpose flour in this recipe.
The point of covering the bowl with a dish towel or cheesecloth is to let air circulate inside the bowl, but to keep any passing houseflies or curious pets out.  Do not use plastic wrap or put a lid on the bowl.
The starter is ready when it becomes very bubbly and has a much larger volume in the 4–12 hours after feeding it.  If you don''t have a lot of bubbles by the fourth day, then you may need to keep going for a few more days (or start all over with a clean bowl).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,292.8,8.72,1.18,0,61.84,0,0,3.97,'B',75,1),
