(31311,'https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook%3AOpenCola','en','CC-BY-SA-3.0','Wikibooks — Cookbook:OpenCola',NULL,NULL,1,'The sugar can be replaced with artificial sweeteners for a diet drink. The opensoda.org formula from 2009 calls for replacement with Splenda at ⅛ the mass of the original sugar amount.
Try measuring the flavoring oils with an eyedropper.
Alcohol can be used to aid with mixing the flavoring. Cube-cola instead uses a kitchen whisk attached to power tools.
Use only food-grade flavoring oils. Note that these oils can cause skin irritation. Wear food-prep or surgical gloves. If oils come in contact with skin, wash with soap and water.
It is very important that you get only food-grade gum arabic, as art-grade can be toxic.
75% phosphoric acid is corrosive to the eyes and skin. Handle with gloved hands, and use extreme caution. If comes in contact with the eyes or skin, immediately flush with plenty of water for at least 15 minutes. Get medical attention. Rinse any spills on clothing or other surfaces thoroughly. Store in a secure area. Do not store more than 50.0 ml.
Caffeine can kill people in relatively small doses. The median lethal dose for an adult human is around 10 grams, or approximately ⅓ ounce. You can find out more by looking up the material safety data sheet (MSDS) for caffeine. Don''t yield to the temptation to create a "Super-Jolt" by adding tons and tons of the white stuff to your cola, or you''ll be in a world of hurt. It''s best not to store caffeine in any amount. If stored, store in a secure area away from children. Absolutely do not put more than three times the amount of caffeine here (when scaling up or down if you are upscaling or downscaling the recipe).
14 drops orange oil
11 drops lime oil
5 drops cassia oil
4 drops lemon oil
4 drops nutmeg oil
1 drop coriander oil
1 drop neroli oil
1 drop lavender oil
2.5 mL (½ teaspoon) food-grade gum arabic
0.6 mL (⅛ teaspoon) water
2¼ cups (532 mL / 472 g / 1.04 lb) plain granulated white table sugar
1¾ cups (456 mL / 0.882 quarts) water
1 teaspoon (5 mL) caramel color
¾ teaspoon (3.45 mL) 75% phosphoric acid or citric acid
⅜ tsp (2 mL) Flavoring Formula
⅛ tsp (0.5 mL) caffeine (optional)','https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Opencola.jpg/960px-Opencola.jpg',640,853,'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Opencola.jpg','Unukorno','CC BY-SA 3.0',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.5),
