Do not serve the same day—leave it to cool overnight, and serve the next day.
You can also freeze it. Like most stews, it will taste even better when you defrost it.
It can be served with mashed potatoes and the onions and carrots from the stew.
One might consider using a pressure cooker, but those are usually quite tall for this recipe. It might work better with a big diameter pot, that''s not too tall, hence the foil and lid recommendation. Besides, a pressure cooker will cook too fast, which is not ideal for a stew.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,0.1667),
